speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, my question is directed to the Prime Minister.
Further to the letter I sent you this morning, I would like to know what you intend to do about my recommendations which are summarized as follows and are intended to put an end to the masquerade in the Senate:
Oral Questions
1-	that, as soon as possible, a Senate code of ethics be implemented that would oblige senators to disclose appointments to the boards of major corporations or banks;
2-	under the authority of the House of Commons to appropriate funds, that the vote of $41 million, representing Senate salaries, be reduced to zero, so that taxpayers would no longer have to pay for all their nonsense;
3-	that, under section 38 of the Canadian Constitution, you initiate a constitutional resolution that would completely abolish the Senate in its present form.
